{"content":[{"c":["ABIEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Father of Kish and Ner and grandfather of King Saul, according to ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.9.1","r":"1Sam.9.1","rawR":"1Sam.9.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.9.1","value":"1Sam.9.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Samuel 9:1"}," and ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.51","r":"1Sam.14.51","rawR":"1Sam.14.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.51","value":"1Sam.14.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:51"},". Other genealogies in 1 Chronicles list Ner, instead of Abiel, as Kish’s father and Saul’s grandfather (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.33","r":"1Chr.8.33","rawR":"1Chr.8.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.33","value":"1Chr.8.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:33"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.39","r":"1Chr.9.39","rawR":"1Chr.9.39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.39","value":"1Chr.9.39"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:39"},"). This confusion is due either to a copyist’s error or to the possibility that Saul had two relatives named Ner, a great-grandfather and an uncle."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Warrior among David’s mighty men who were known as “the thirty” (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.11.32","r":"1Chr.11.32","rawR":"1Chr.11.32","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.11.32","value":"1Chr.11.32"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 11:32"},"), also called Abi-albon the Arbathite (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.23.31","r":"2Sam.23.31","rawR":"2Sam.23.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.23.31","value":"2Sam.23.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 23:31"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Abiel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Samuel 9:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.9.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.9.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.9.1"},{"anchorText":"14:51","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.51","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.51","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.51"},